---Attach a Change to a Trail
---
---Makes existing repository code work an owned Change under its stable Change ID. The Change's repository must be in the Trail's scope, and the caller needs both project write and repository push access. Attachment is idempotent: a replay for the same Trail returns the same Change and Location with 201.
---
---`PUT /api/v1/{host}/{project}/trails/{trailId}/changes/{changeId}`
---@param input entire.project_trails.AttachTrailChangeRequest
---@return entire.project_trails.ChangeSummaryResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:attach_trail_change(input) end

---Start a project Trail discussion
---
---Creates a discussion and its first message under this project Trail. Requires project management or push on a repository in the Trail's current stored scope; does not create repository work, advance the parent metadata ETag, or run code-review automation.
---
---`POST /api/v1/{host}/{project}/trails/{trailId}/discussions`
---@param input entire.project_trails.CreateProjectDiscussionRequest
---@return entire.project_trails.DiscussionCreateResponseBody? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_project_discussion(input) end

---Reply to a project Trail discussion
---
---Replies to a discussion owned by this project Trail. Requires project management or stored-scope repository push, and discussion containment; preserves the shared message response contract.
---
---`POST /api/v1/{host}/{project}/trails/{trailId}/discussions/{discussionId}/messages`
---@param input entire.project_trails.CreateProjectDiscussionMessageRequest
---@return entire.project_trails.TrailDiscussionMessageResponseBody? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_project_discussion_message(input) end

---Create a project trail
---
---Repo writers need push (an automation: push or write_trails) on every repository in a nonempty project scope. Automations cannot set assignees. Unscoped creation and initial Changes require project management. Initial Changes require Idempotency-Key; database writes are atomic, Git refs are not.
---
---`POST /api/v1/{host}/{project}/trails`
---@param input entire.project_trails.CreateProjectTrailRequest
---@return entire.project_trails.TrailResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_project_trail(input) end

---Create a Change within a Trail
---
---Create a new branch-backed Change, or use branchAction=link to reuse existing repository work. Linking preserves existing fields, returns same-parent work unchanged, and rejects another parent. Creation fields are validated but only applied to new work. A legacy body field is ignored; descriptions belong to the project Trail. Trail editors with write access to a repository in the same project may create Changes and add that repository to the scope. Scope removal/replacement remains project-managed.
---
---`POST /api/v1/{host}/{project}/trails/{trailId}/changes`
---@param input entire.project_trails.CreateTrailChangeRequest
---@return entire.project_trails.TrailChangeCreateOutputBody? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_trail_change(input) end

