---List repositories with Trails enabled in one project
---
---Returns repositories owned by exactly one required project_id with Trails enabled whose processing-primary placement is recorded in this cell, including repositories with no Trails yet. Only repositories the caller can read (repo/pull, or an automation's read_trails) are returned; project authority does not bypass repository access. Only the processing-primary placement is returned for each repo group; secondary placements are never used as a fallback. Read-time permission filtering may temporarily omit newly granted repositories; when the readable set is empty, repository denials are rechecked at full consistency before the empty-list or 404 decision. Results contain id, full_name, and forge, ordered by case-insensitive full_name then id, with no pagination. Project viewers/managers receive an empty repositories array when none are readable and enabled; other callers receive 404. Use the project's jurisdiction, as for GET /trails.
---
---`GET /api/v1/trails/repos`
---@param input entire.project_trails.ListProjectTrailRepositoriesRequest
---@return entire.project_trails.ProjectTrailRepositoriesResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_project_trail_repositories(input) end

